WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.773
- [Swamp Ape] Alright, everybody ready?

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.430
Just stretch him out.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.530
- This is a hatchling.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.400
This is a brand new snake.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.620
This was born this year, and
this is maybe a month old.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.270
Within five years, this'll be 12-13 feet.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.920
It's amazing how quick they grow.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.140
The Swamp Apes take
veterans into the Everglades

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:25.130
to track and capture Burmese pythons.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.810
We help the veterans
overcome their challenges

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.900
from their service.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.640
At the same time, the wilderness benefits

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.340
from the removal of these animals.

00:00:38.172 --> 00:00:41.422
(gentle marimba music)

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.140
My name is Tom Rahill. I
founded the Swamp Apes.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.950
The Swamp Apes are an organization

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:50.500
dedicated to serving veterans
who serve in the wilderness.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.700
The Everglades is renowned
for it biological diversity,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.230
it's under threat by the Burmese pythons.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.700
- [Swamp Ape] One more
python out of our Everglades.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.700
- The Burmese pythons have
decimated the mammal population;

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.503
that's their primary food source.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.630
It's estimated that there
are over 100,000 pythons

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.140
in the Everglades.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.463
The Swamp Apes have captured
and removed over 1,000 pythons.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.710
The Burmese pythons,
largely, were released

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.969
by irresponsible pet owners.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:23.970
(Swamp Apes yelling)

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.010
- [Swamp Ape] Hang on, we got something.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.250
- [Tom] A 15-foot python
could have 60 hatches,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.663
and it's just an exponential problem.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.060
The hope is to remove enough
of the breeding females

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.603
that we can severely
diminish the population.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.875
(upbeat music)

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:44.520
During the wet season, which we're in now,

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.190
the technique for capturing
pythons is road-cruising.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.930
At night, when it's a little
moist out, reptiles come out

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.610
onto the road.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.010
We have a policy of live
capture with the pythons.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.110
We effectively jump on the pythons.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:59.030
- [Swamp Ape] That's
a nice sized one, too.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.730
- [Tom] You grab them as soon
as you can behind the head.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.850
That business end of a
python can be very dangerous.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.270
We turn them over to the scientists;

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.460
sadly, 99-percent of these
animals have to be euthanized.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.340
- That's a whole population
of native critters

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.390
that are being saved.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.470
- The Swamp Apes began in
2008, for me, as a tool

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.610
to deal with some personal grief.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.320
When my wife moved to Arkansas
to take a teaching job,

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.480
I'd only see her once every month or two.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.900
Consequently, I was hurtin' emotionally.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.890
And I went and started volunteering

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:34.610
in the Everglades National Park.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.040
I then was invited to join
the python eradication team,

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.750
and at a certain point it occurred to me

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.220
that this would be great for veterans also

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.043
with PTSD and other challenges.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.020
The Swamp Apes are a unique program:

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.730
we embrace the veteran skillset.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.160
Basic training for a veteran

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.464
would include situational-awareness,

00:02:56.464 --> 00:03:01.260
threat-assessment,
self-reliance, chain-of-command,

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.420
mission-focus.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.800
- You got your mojo working man.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.925
- [Tom] Once they get out of the service,

00:03:05.925 --> 00:03:06.758
they don't necessarily

00:03:06.758 --> 00:03:10.890
have a place to apply the basic training,

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.880
let alone specialized training.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.370
Swamp Apes use that training
and celebrate that training,

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:19.750
and the veterans service, by
applying it to python removal.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.380
- [Swamp Ape] Why don't you come with me?

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.177
Ow, he bit my hand.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:31.790
- [Tom] We have positively
impacted hundreds of veterans

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:33.080
with the program.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.930
They benefit from the natural
therapy of being out there,

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:39.188
tracking, capturing, and
removing the pythons.

00:03:39.188 --> 00:03:41.870
(bird calling)

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.360
- [Swamp Ape] Come on pretty girl.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.980
- Our ultimate goal is to have therapists

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.910
accompany us, and be a
prescribable therapy organization.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:53.910
As noble and as effective as
the Swamp Apes are in engaging

00:03:54.047 --> 00:03:56.520
veterans, at the end of the day,

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.280
we get to jump on big snakes.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.113
It's awesome.

00:04:00.104 --> 00:04:03.771
(acoustic guitar strumming)

